-- title:
--   Kechris Thm 17.24 — the Borel σ-algebra of the weak topology on $P(X)$ is the Giry σ-algebra
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be a separable (pseudo-)metrizable space with its Borel $\sigma$-algebra and let $P(X)$ be the space of Borel probability measures on $X$ with the weak topology. Then the Borel $\sigma$-algebra of $P(X)$ coincides with the $\sigma$-algebra generated by the evaluation maps $\mu\mapsto\mu(A)$, $A\subseteq X$ Borel (the Giry $\sigma$-algebra, which is Mathlib's `MeasurableSpace` instance on `ProbabilityMeasure X`).
--
--   This is Kechris, Theorem 17.24, which states that the Borel space of $P(X)$ is generated by the maps $\mu\mapsto\mu(U)$, $U$ open, and equivalently by the maps $\mu\mapsto\mu(A)$, $A$ Borel.
-- source:
--   A. S. Kechris, Classical Descriptive Set Theory (GTM 156, Springer 1995), §17.E, Theorem 17.24

import Mathlib

open MeasureTheory

/-- Kechris, Classical Descriptive Set Theory, Theorem 17.24: if `X` is separable metrizable,
the Borel σ-algebra of the weak topology on `P(X)` is generated by the maps `μ ↦ μ(A)`,
`A` Borel; i.e. it coincides with the Giry σ-algebra. -/
theorem ProbabilityMeasureSpace.borelSpace {X : Type*} [TopologicalSpace X]
    [TopologicalSpace.PseudoMetrizableSpace X] [TopologicalSpace.SeparableSpace X]
    [MeasurableSpace X] [BorelSpace X] :
    BorelSpace (ProbabilityMeasure X) := by sorry
